{
  "info": {
    "name": "Message Broker",
    "description": "Message Broker - Team 17 \"Student ID, please\" (Lab 4).\n\nThe internal component between the Gateway and the services, and between the services for events. It is not routed through the Gateway, so these requests go to the broker directly, on the port the team's Compose file publishes (localhost:8100).\n\nCovers forwarding a request to the least loaded instance, publishing an event and its delivery to the subscribing service, the duplicate and error answers of /publish, the topics, a dead letter, the logs download and the metrics.\n\nRun the team's docker-compose.yml first. Requests are ordered to run start to finish: the event published in \"Events\" is checked on Credential Service at the end of that folder, and the event refused in \"Topics and dead letters\" is found in the dead letters and counted in the metrics.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health and logs",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{broker_url}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{broker_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The broker's own state, in the same shape as every service's /health."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('the broker is UP', () => pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('UP'));",
                  "pm.test('it names itself', () => pm.expect(body.service).to.eql('message-broker'));",
                  "pm.test('it reports its load', () => pm.expect(body.load.utilization).to.be.within(0, 1));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
